WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.567
-Pro-Trump
January 6th conspirator

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:05.300
Jim Jordan
lost a second bid

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.667
to become
the Speaker of the House today,

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:08.200
receiving even fewer votes

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.067
than he got
on the first ballot yesterday,

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:12.667
leaving Republicans
in total chaos

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:14.334
and no closer
to resolving their crisis

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:15.667
than they were
two weeks ago.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:18.167
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:21.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.434 --> 00:00:24.634
We're now going on two weeks
without a Speaker of the House,

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:26.300
meaning one of our two chambers
of Congress

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.300
is completely paralyzed
and can't do anything.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.167
Jordan lost one ballot yesterday
and then another today.

00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:33.200
In fact,
after today's failed ballot,

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.400
the temporary Speaker,
Patrick McHenry,

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.334
immediately gaveled the House
back into recess.

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:41.334
-Pursuant to clause 12(a)
of Rule I,

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:43.434
the chair declares
the House in recess,

00:00:43.434 --> 00:00:46.667
subject to the call
of the chair.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.334
-"We took one vote
and [bleep] it up.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:51.667
I'd say let's call it a day."

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:53.767
It's like if the first kid
in a Little League game

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:54.934
struck out
and the coach said,

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:57.567
"Ah, hell with this
same old [bleep]

00:00:57.567 --> 00:01:00.334
We forfeit!

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:01.667
"Tyler's our best hitter!

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:04.701
If he strikes out,
we're [bleep]"

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.701
Although McHenry seems to have
gotten a note

00:01:07.701 --> 00:01:11.300
to tone down his gavel bang,
compared to two weeks ago

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.133
when he was so mad
he nearly broke the dais.

00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:15.133
[ Gavel bangs ]

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:20.701
Is he gaveling the House
into recess,

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:24.367
or did he just see a
New York City bathtub cockroach?

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.267
You know the kind --
they just sort of dance

00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:30.234
around the edge of the drain
as if to say, "That's right.

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:33.400
I live here all the time."

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.968
McHenry's gavel is the sound
the coyote makes

00:01:35.968 --> 00:01:37.467
whenever he falls off a cliff.

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:39.367
-Meep-meep!

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.367
[ High-pitched whistling ]

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.400
[ Gavel bangs ]

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:50.701
-So, the House still
has no Speaker.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:52.901
And for all the Republican
complaints about Biden --

00:01:52.901 --> 00:01:55.567
he's too old, he's too woke,
he's too weak --

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.000
even they have to admit,

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.067
he's a sentient being
who exists.

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:02.000
And the Republicans
can't even deliver that,

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.400
which at the very least,
gives us a chance to update

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.734
our ongoing montage
of House Republican chaos.

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:08.200
And while we do that,

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:12.367
I'm gonna take a few sips
from this bottle of whiskey.

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:15.767
-Kevin McCarthy practically
daring hardline Republicans

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.167
to come after him.

00:02:17.167 --> 00:02:20.367
-If somebody wants to make
a motion against me, bring it.

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:23.367
-To which Gaetz responded,
"Just did."

00:02:23.367 --> 00:02:25.334
-He says he's coming for you.
Can you survive?

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:26.834
-Yes. I'll survive.

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:29.934
-The Speaker of the House has
been removed from his position.

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:33.234
-Some House Republicans
have been in contact with

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:34.734
and have started an effort

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:37.200
to draft former
President Donald Trump

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.367
to be the next Speaker.

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:43.567
-Donald Trump has
just endorsed Jim Jordan

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:45.734
to be the next
Speaker of the House.

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:47.467
-On Capitol Hill right now,
we have breaking news.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:50.300
House Republicans have nominated
Steve Scalise

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.300
moments ago
as their new Speaker.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:55.167
-I want to thank my House
Republican colleagues

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:58.501
for just designating me
as the Speaker.

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:00.834
-Just hours after
being nominated to become

00:03:00.834 --> 00:03:02.567
the next Speaker
of the House,

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:05.901
Congressman Steve Scalise says
he's dropping out of the race.

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:07.400
-I'm withdrawing my name

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:10.200
as a candidate
for the Speaker designee.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:15.000
-Jim Jordan is the new
Republican nominee for Speaker.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.334
-Jim Jordan is trying
to rally support

00:03:17.334 --> 00:03:19.467
ahead of a planned vote today.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.234
-My prediction is
Jim will win this,

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:24.868
and even on the first
round of votes.

00:03:24.868 --> 00:03:26.367
-Congressman Jim Jordan lost

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:27.801
the first vote
for House Speaker.

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:29.200
-A Speaker has not been elected.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.467
-Jim Jordan plans to take
his second shot

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.767
at the speakership
on the House floor.

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:35.667
-Congressman Jim Jordan
appears to have lost

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:37.501
the second round
of votes for Speaker.

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:40.968
-A Speaker has not been elected.

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:42.968
-You probably thought
this bottle would be empty

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:44.400
after that long montage.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.667
Well, it's not.

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:48.334
Because this is
the second bottle.

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:50.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:51.968
So, the House still
has no Speaker.

00:03:51.968 --> 00:03:54.133
In fact, Jordan actually
lost more votes

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.100
on today's ballot
than he did on yesterday's.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.567
As evidence of how bad
it's getting,

00:03:57.567 --> 00:04:01.501
one GOP member of Congress voted
for a former Republican Speaker

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:05.634
who has been extremely vocal
about how much he hated the job.

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:09.033
-We really are sort of in
silly season with some of this.

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:15.033
Congressman Mike Kelly voted
for former Speaker Boehner.

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:16.534
-If John Boehner
found out someone

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:18.000
was trying
to make him Speaker again,

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.634
he would immediately
burst into tears.

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:23.467
Remember that? Boehner crying?
'Cause that was a thing.

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:26.300
And that's today's topical
reference from 10 years ago.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.000
Besides, Boehner --
and this is true --

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.300
is super into weed now.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.434
He became a cannabis
entrepreneur after he retired.

00:04:33.434 --> 00:04:34.834
That's how long the [bleep] show

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:35.934
in the House Republican
Conference

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:37.400
has been going on.
That was so long ago

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.200
that when we did a piece
on Boehner resigning,

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.200
I looked like this.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.767
If you were to compare
how Boehner looks now

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:44.968
to how I look now,
you would definitely assume

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:48.067
I was the one
who got super into weed.

00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:49.968
No more suits, man.
I'm wearing a cardigan

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:52.334
and growing my hair out
to look like The Dude.

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:54.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.300
So, Jordan lost a second,
humiliating vote,

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.067
and we're going on two weeks
without a functioning

00:04:58.067 --> 00:05:00.234
House of Representatives,
and everyone is pissed about it.

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:03.234
Especially Republicans, who keep
admitting that this spectacle

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:05.901
is making them look like
a bunch of incompetent morons.

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:08.801
-Funding the government
is part of our fundamental duty,

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:10.267
and we can't even do that.

00:05:10.267 --> 00:05:12.968
It's bordering
on the -- on the absurd.

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:14.133
-This is petty.

00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:15.367
-This is not responsible.

00:05:15.367 --> 00:05:17.534
-Makes us look like
a bunch of idiots.

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:20.033
-We keep playing those clips
because they're the ones

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:22.734
saying all the stuff
we usually say about them.

00:05:22.734 --> 00:05:25.601
They're doing their own
"Closer Look" about themselves.

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:28.434
Soon, Rudy Giuliani
is gonna go on Fox News

00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:30.200
and say, "You know what
I just realized?

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.300
I look like I sat on my balls."

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:41.501
Seriously, Republicans are
making all of our points for us.

00:05:41.501 --> 00:05:43.834
At this point, we don't even
need to do any writing.

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:45.667
Wally's cue cards
are all blank.

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:47.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.634
Hey, Wally, sometimes you have
lines on the show, right?

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:51.467
-Yeah, that's right.
-And when you do,

00:05:51.467 --> 00:05:52.834
one of the other cue card guys

00:05:52.834 --> 00:05:54.567
holds your cue cards?
-That's correct.

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:56.200
-But the other day,
you had the line,

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:57.801
"Well, Seth,"
before I cut you off.

00:05:57.801 --> 00:05:59.501
And I'm just wondering,
do you have cue cards

00:05:59.501 --> 00:06:01.067
when your line is that short?

00:06:01.067 --> 00:06:02.300
-No, no, I just remember it.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.634
-Yeah, that makes sense.

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:05.734
Republicans are --

00:06:05.734 --> 00:06:08.868
So you can memorize a line
that short?

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:09.968
-Sure.

00:06:09.968 --> 00:06:11.501
-Because when the editors
were looking

00:06:11.501 --> 00:06:12.734
at Monday's "Closer Look,"

00:06:12.734 --> 00:06:14.267
they noticed something
was written on your hand.

00:06:14.267 --> 00:06:16.767
And when they zoomed in,
they saw this.

00:06:16.767 --> 00:06:19.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.033 --> 00:06:22.534
So...

00:06:22.534 --> 00:06:25.267
-Yeah, that was
for something else.

00:06:25.267 --> 00:06:27.100
-That was for something else?
-Yeah.

00:06:27.100 --> 00:06:28.434
I always write little notes
on my hand.

00:06:28.434 --> 00:06:30.167
Want to see mine today?
-Yeah, sure.

00:06:31.934 --> 00:06:34.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.267 --> 00:06:35.434
Alright.

00:06:35.434 --> 00:06:37.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:40.033
Oh, good.

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:41.868
And it's not just
Republican politicians.

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.534
Conservative pundits
are also mad at them.

00:06:43.534 --> 00:06:46.634
Not mad at them for nominating
an election denier

00:06:46.634 --> 00:06:48.567
and coup plotter
like Jim Jordan, mind you,

00:06:48.567 --> 00:06:50.734
but for not
lining up behind him.

00:06:50.734 --> 00:06:53.334
Fox host Brian Kilmeade
was caught on a hot mic

00:06:53.334 --> 00:06:56.033
during yesterday's vote,
insulting one member of Congress

00:06:56.033 --> 00:06:58.534
who chose not to vote
for Jim Jordan.

00:06:58.534 --> 00:06:59.868
Kilmeade's not on screen,

00:06:59.868 --> 00:07:02.267
so listen for his comment
at the end.

00:07:02.267 --> 00:07:04.100
-Bacon.
-McCarthy.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.100
-McCarthy.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:11.701
-Dumbass.

00:07:11.701 --> 00:07:14.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:18.267
-Even worse, he had to write
that line on his hand.

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:19.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:21.334
Do you know how bad
things are for you

00:07:21.334 --> 00:07:23.734
when Brian Kilmeade
is calling you a dumbass?

00:07:23.734 --> 00:07:25.133
This is a guy so dumb,

00:07:25.133 --> 00:07:28.801
he once tried to roast
a marshmallow over an open flame

00:07:28.801 --> 00:07:30.267
with a plastic spoon.

00:07:30.267 --> 00:07:31.901
-I got the marshmallows.

00:07:31.901 --> 00:07:34.467
-Alright, while Steve roasts
his marshmallows...

00:07:34.467 --> 00:07:36.133
Watch. Watch your fingers.
-That's a little dangerous.

00:07:36.133 --> 00:07:37.467
-They're small.

00:07:37.467 --> 00:07:39.868
They're a little small.
Can we get a stick?

00:07:39.868 --> 00:07:41.434
Anybody got a stick?
[ Indistinct chatter ]

00:07:41.434 --> 00:07:43.901
Ouch! That's hot.

00:07:43.901 --> 00:07:45.367
Ouch!

00:07:45.367 --> 00:07:47.234
-You're really gonna do that
with your hands?

00:07:47.234 --> 00:07:48.868
You're not gonna...?
-Yeah, you're right.

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:51.367
Upon further review,
we're looking for a stick.

00:07:51.367 --> 00:07:53.734
-Oh, plastic!
-No, no, no! Not plastic!

00:07:53.734 --> 00:07:55.701
That's bad for the environment.

00:07:55.701 --> 00:07:57.667
[ Laughter ]

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:05.868
-So, Steve Doocy tried
to use his hand

00:08:05.868 --> 00:08:09.367
to roast
a cocoa-sized marshmallow.

00:08:09.367 --> 00:08:11.701
Then Kilmeade said,
"No, I've got a better idea.

00:08:11.701 --> 00:08:14.000
How about plastic?"

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.868
We have an annual fire safety
training here at 30 Rock,

00:08:16.868 --> 00:08:19.434
and never once has the
fire marshal thought to tell us,

00:08:19.434 --> 00:08:22.133
"Don't stick a plastic spoon
into an open flame."

00:08:22.133 --> 00:08:23.968
Meanwhile, the fire marshal
at Fox &amp; Friends

00:08:23.968 --> 00:08:26.334
has to clarify that
when you use the fire escape,

00:08:26.334 --> 00:08:28.701
you want to make sure
you go down.

00:08:28.701 --> 00:08:30.367
[ Laughter ]

00:08:30.367 --> 00:08:32.501
By the way, just to give you
an idea of how much worse

00:08:32.501 --> 00:08:35.033
Fox News has gotten
in the 13 years since that clip,

00:08:35.033 --> 00:08:38.000
the only two people in that clip
still employed by the network

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.934
are the guys who tried to roast
a marshmallow

00:08:39.934 --> 00:08:42.834
with their hands
and a plastic spoon.

00:08:42.834 --> 00:08:45.400
But the role of Fox News here
goes beyond muttered insults,

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.200
because it turns out some of
the right-wing personalities

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.868
have been pressuring
Republican holdouts

00:08:49.868 --> 00:08:51.567
to back Jordan,
including Sean Hannity.

00:08:51.567 --> 00:08:54.200
And now that pressure campaign
seems to have backfired,

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.534
making Republicans even angrier.

00:08:55.534 --> 00:08:56.901
On his radio show this week,

00:08:56.901 --> 00:08:59.234
Hannity took exception
to the allegation

00:08:59.234 --> 00:09:01.634
that he was trying to influence
Republicans to back Jordan.

00:09:45.968 --> 00:09:48.400
-Yeah.
He's like the entire newspaper.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.200
You should see his funny pages.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:52.367
[ Laughter ]

00:09:52.367 --> 00:09:54.200
So, why are conservative
hardliners

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:55.767
pressuring everyone
to vote for Jordan?

00:09:55.767 --> 00:09:58.200
Because Trump backs Jordan
and Jordan backs Trump.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.334
Jordan was a key player
in the January 6th coup attempt

00:10:00.334 --> 00:10:02.100
and still to this day
refuses to say

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:03.968
that the 2020 election
was not stolen.

00:10:03.968 --> 00:10:06.167
He was named throughout
the congressional report

00:10:06.167 --> 00:10:07.767
on the insurrection
as a key player,

00:10:07.767 --> 00:10:09.801
defied a subpoena
to answer questions,

00:10:09.801 --> 00:10:11.501
and was listed on
the president's call sheet

00:10:11.501 --> 00:10:12.834
from that day.

00:10:12.834 --> 00:10:14.234
According to a copy obtained
by The Washington Post,

00:10:14.234 --> 00:10:16.067
the schedule says
that at 9:24 a.m.,

00:10:16.067 --> 00:10:18.534
the President talked
with Representative Jim Jordan.

00:10:18.534 --> 00:10:20.567
But Jordan initially refused
to answer questions

00:10:20.567 --> 00:10:23.100
about whether he spoke
with Trump on January 6th,

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:25.767
leading to this very awkward
interview with a reporter.

00:10:25.767 --> 00:10:27.067
-Yes or no?

00:10:27.067 --> 00:10:30.100
Did you speak with
President Trump on January 6th?

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.334
-Yeah, I mean, I speak-- I spoke
with the president last week.

00:10:32.334 --> 00:10:33.467
I speak with the president
all the time.

00:10:33.467 --> 00:10:34.901
I spoke with him
on January 6th.

00:10:34.901 --> 00:10:37.400
I mean, I talk with
President Trump all the time.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.400
Uh, I-I-I'm actually
kind of amazed

00:10:39.400 --> 00:10:40.701
sometimes that people
keep asking this que--

00:10:40.701 --> 00:10:42.167
Of course, I talk with
the president all the time.

00:10:42.167 --> 00:10:44.100
I talk with him -- Like I said,
I talked with him last week.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.767
-On January 6th,
did you speak with him before,

00:10:46.767 --> 00:10:50.267
during, or after
the Capitol was attacked?

00:10:50.267 --> 00:10:52.501
-Uh, I'd have to go...
I-I-I...

00:10:52.501 --> 00:10:54.767
I spoke with him
that day...after?

00:10:54.767 --> 00:10:56.167
I think after.

00:10:56.167 --> 00:10:58.167
I don't know if I spoke with him
in the morning or not.

00:10:58.167 --> 00:11:00.300
I-I just don't know.
Uh, I'd have to go back and...

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:03.567
I-I mean, I don't -- I don't --
I don't know, uh, th-that,

00:11:03.567 --> 00:11:05.734
w-when -- when those
conversations happened.

00:11:05.734 --> 00:11:07.067
-When someone talks that fast,

00:11:07.067 --> 00:11:09.100
they're either holding
an auction, lying their ass off,

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:11.100
or pitching a screenplay
at a Malibu beach house

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.434
after snorting
a mountain of blow.

00:11:13.434 --> 00:11:15.200
By the way, congrats
to that reporter for remaining

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:17.601
completely still and just
letting Jordan spin out.

00:11:17.601 --> 00:11:20.133
That's how you do it.

00:11:20.133 --> 00:11:22.901
Just sit there motionless while
he picks up speed

00:11:22.901 --> 00:11:25.067
like a bull[bleep] bobsledder.

00:11:25.067 --> 00:11:26.067
[ Laughter ]

00:11:26.067 --> 00:11:27.501
Jordan was talking so fast,

00:11:27.501 --> 00:11:29.000
the only way you could
slow him down

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.334
is if one of his fellow
Republicans

00:11:30.334 --> 00:11:31.834
knocked him over the head
like this.

00:11:31.834 --> 00:11:33.167
[ Gavel bangs ]

00:11:33.167 --> 00:11:34.834
[ Laughter ]

00:11:34.834 --> 00:11:36.400
Trump and his allies
want Jordan in charge

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:38.000
so they can take another crack
at what they tried

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.367
and failed to do on January 6th.

00:11:39.367 --> 00:11:41.667
The other problem is,
no one sane wants to be Speaker

00:11:41.667 --> 00:11:43.000
because it's a horrible job

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.033
where you have to deal
with lunatics like Jim Jordan --

00:11:45.033 --> 00:11:47.133
leaving an opening for lunatics
like Jim Jordan.

00:11:47.133 --> 00:11:49.300
In fact, here's
how much the job

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:51.300
of being a Republican
Speaker of the House sucks.

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:53.067
One GOP congressman,
Ken Buck,

00:11:53.067 --> 00:11:55.334
who has simply asked
that any future Speaker

00:11:55.334 --> 00:11:57.033
admit Biden fairly won
the election,

00:11:57.033 --> 00:11:59.434
joked on CNN that he voted
for someone

00:11:59.434 --> 00:12:02.200
he knows for a fact
wouldn't want the job.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.000
-Joining me now
is Republican Congressman

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.601
Ken Buck of Colorado.

00:12:05.601 --> 00:12:08.767
He did not vote
for Congressman Jim Jordan,

00:12:08.767 --> 00:12:10.501
instead voting
for Tom Emmer.

00:12:10.501 --> 00:12:12.133
Well, I guess
my first question is,

00:12:12.133 --> 00:12:14.300
do you really want Tom Emmer
to be Speaker?

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:15.934
-No, I don't.
I don't like Tom Emmer.

00:12:15.934 --> 00:12:17.834
I figured this would be
the worst job in America.

00:12:17.834 --> 00:12:20.167
-Okay, so just
to underscore that,

00:12:20.167 --> 00:12:22.000
you voted for somebody

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:24.067
because you don't like them.

00:12:24.067 --> 00:12:25.734
-I-I voted for somebody
'cause I wasn't gonna vote

00:12:25.734 --> 00:12:27.434
for Jim Jordan.
-Yeah, but -- but you don't...

00:12:27.434 --> 00:12:29.267
It's not because you want him
to be Speaker.

00:12:29.267 --> 00:12:31.434
Okay, well, that says a lot
about where we are right now.

00:12:31.434 --> 00:12:32.901
[ Laughter ]

00:12:32.901 --> 00:12:35.200
-He voted for someone
who doesn't want to be Speaker

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:37.067
because the job
of Speaker sucks.

00:12:37.067 --> 00:12:39.100
It's third in line
to the presidency,

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:41.000
and Republicans are treating it
like it's a punishment

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:43.000
on "Impractical Jokers."

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.334
And at this point, why not?

00:12:44.334 --> 00:12:46.534
Give the gavel to Murr and let
the other jokers tell him

00:12:46.534 --> 00:12:48.033
what to do with it
through an earpiece

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:50.234
while they watch
from inside a van.

00:12:50.234 --> 00:12:52.601
"Bang it so hard
you break the podium."

00:12:52.601 --> 00:12:54.100
The fundamental problem here
is that

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:55.701
the GOP is
a fractured coalition

00:12:55.701 --> 00:12:57.834
with no discernible
ideological core,

00:12:57.834 --> 00:13:00.901
except that most of them want
to dismantle American democracy.

00:13:00.901 --> 00:13:03.667
And on top of that, the job
of Speaker absolutely sucks.

00:13:03.667 --> 00:13:05.133
In order to want it, you'd have
to be a...

00:13:05.133 --> 00:13:06.200
-Petty...
-Absurd...

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:07.701
-Dumbass.

00:13:07.701 --> 00:13:09.701
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:13:09.701 --> 00:13:11.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

